--- THE RESULT SYNTHESIS PIPELINE (added 2026-09-26, Sec. 3.8) ---
fold | one of five time-ordered parts of one participant's windows; each fold holds about one fifth of the SKIP windows; each fold serves once as test data | Sec. Temporal Cross-Validation and Data Balancing
fold gap | the 3 s dropped around each fold border (every window starting within 1.5 s of the border is dropped); window starts of training and test data lie more than 3 s apart, i.e. more than 2 s without any window between them (do NOT say "3 s between windows"; do NOT use "firewall" or "safety distance") | Sec. Temporal Cross-Validation and Data Balancing
seed | the starting number of the random generator that picks the dropped windows in balancing; five seeds (0, 1, 7, 42, 99); intra-subject results average over the five seeds, inter-subject uses the first seed only | Sec. Temporal Cross-Validation and Data Balancing
balancing | randomly dropping windows of the LARGER class (STAY in 21 of 25 participants; SKIP in P17, P23, P24, P28), separately in every training fold and every test fold (do NOT say "STAY was undersampled per participant") | Sec. Temporal Cross-Validation and Data Balancing
EI model / top-feature model | logistic regression with the EI, or with one top feature, as the only input | Sec. Logistic Regression Modeling and Baselines
one-sided model | a model that calls nearly every window one class; high recall for that class, chance precision; the inter-subject EI model calls about 90% of all windows STAY (do NOT say the EI 'detects STAY well') | Sec. Metrics and Significance Testing / EI Model versus Coin-Flip Baseline
|d| | the size of Cohen's d; the EI reaches 0.022; TP10 raw standard deviation 0.196 = about nine times the EI (do NOT say 'tenfold') | Sec. Class Separation of Single Features
F1-train / F1-test | F1-score on training windows / on test windows; metrics are computed per participant from TP, TN, FP, FN summed over all folds and seeds (NOT "per fold") | Sec. Metrics and Significance Testing
student who has seen the exam questions | mental image for leakage between training and test data; coined in Sec. Adjacent Study, reused in Sec. Temporal Cross-Validation | Sec. Adjacent Study
--- DISCUSSION (added 2026-09-28, Sec. 4.5) ---
chance-equivalent reference | RETIRED (2026-09-28): undefined in the Results; say 'the chance level of about 50%' | Sec. Discussion
two singers | mental image for EMG and EEG sharing frequencies, so a filter cannot pull them apart; coined in Sec. EMG Artifacts in EEG, reused once in Sec. Discussion | Sec. EMG Artifacts in EEG
height analogy | why |d| below 0.2 still predicts near chance: two groups of adults whose average height differs by one or two centimetres | Sec. Discussion
adapted EI | the EI of this thesis (variance of z-scored envelope, AF7/AF8/TP9/TP10, beta 13-30 Hz), as opposed to Pope et al.'s band-power EI at Cz/Pz/P3/P4, beta 13-22 Hz | Sec. Engagement Index / Discussion
